.TH HOMELAB-CLI-DRIVE 8 "2026-08-21" "homelab-cli" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
homelab-cli\-drive \- Drive (file/directory/share) commands for homelab\-cli
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B homelab-cli
.RB [ --api-url
.IR url ]
.B drive
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B homelab-cli drive
groups every Drive-related REST call under one command family. All
subcommands require a saved login (see
.BR homelab-cli (8)) except the public-share commands, which take a
share token instead and need no authentication.
.P
Run
.RI "\(lqhomelab-cli drive " command " --help\(rq"
for a given subcommand's own arguments; this page only summarizes what
each one does.
.SH "PUBLIC SHARES (NO AUTH)"
.TP
.B share-meta
Get metadata for a public file share link.
.TP
.B share-dir
Get metadata and file list for a public directory share link.
.TP
.B share-download
Download a file via a public share link.
.SH "FILES AND DIRECTORIES"
.TP
.B quota
Show usage/limit/file count for the current user.
.TP
.BR file-info ", " file-meta ", " file-versions
List files by path or directory id, show lightweight metadata for one
file, or list all of a file's versions.
.TP
.BR upload-file ", " download-file
Upload a local file, or download a file's content.
.TP
.BR trash-file ", " move-file ", " copy-file
Soft-delete, move/rename, or queue an async copy of a file.
.TP
.BR list-trash ", " restore-file ", " empty-trash ", " trash-dir
List trashed files, restore one, permanently empty Trash, or get/create
the user's Trash directory id.
.TP
.BR list-directories ", " create-directory ", " delete-directory ", " update-directory
Directory CRUD: list, create, recursively delete, move/rename.
.SH "SHARING AND BULK OPERATIONS"
.TP
.BR share-file ", " share-directory
Create a share for a file or directory (omit
.B --share-with
for a public link).
.TP
.BR list-shares ", " list-shares-with-me ", " delete-share
List shares you created, shares others created targeting you, or
revoke a share you own.
.TP
.BR bulk-trash ", " bulk-restore ", " bulk-move ", " bulk-copy
Operate on multiple files/directories at once.
.TP
.B create-zip
Queue an async zip of files/directories into a destination directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR homelab-cli (8),
.BR homelab-cli-mail (8),
.BR homelab-cli-admin (8)
